==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ar}} {{Arab|[[حسن|حَسَن]]}} meaning fine, good, good-looking, handsome, manly or strong.

===Proper noun===
{{wikipedia|Hasan bin Ali}}
'''Hassan''' or '''Hasan'''

# The name Hassan in Arabic comes from Hassan the first son of [[Ali]] and brother of [[Husein]]; the second [[Shiite]] [[Imam]]
# The name Hassan may have an eastern look but in [[Ireland]] it is the anglicized form of Ó hOsáin.
# The name Hassan in [[Hebrew]] '''חסן''' means "cantor", or "good cantor" derived from the Arabic "good" and the Hebrew "cantor"

